# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Without it, the line endings of a file depend on whichever editor wrote it
# last: Git for Windows, Cline/Mimo, Notepad and an AI agent's edit tool all
# disagree, and nothing in the repository says who is right.
#
# That has already cost us real time twice. A one-line version bump turned into
# an 11,752-line diff in main.py, and a one-line assertion change turned into a
# 910-line diff in tests/test_price_sweep.py - in both cases the whole file was
# rewritten from LF to CRLF, so the actual change was invisible in review and
# would have collided with any second session editing the same files.
#
# This file pins the policy INSIDE the repository, so it applies identically on
# Windows, in CI, on Render and in every editor - it does not depend on any
# per-machine git config (core.autocrlf), which is what made the behaviour
# unpredictable before.

# Text files: stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never normalise these, never touch a byte.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.webp    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.mp4     binary
*.mov     binary
*.zip     binary
*.gz      binary
*.db      binary
*.sqlite  binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.pdf     binary

# Scalable vector graphics are text and should stay that way.
*.svg     text eol=lf
